/-!
# Stacks 0BXD: `Mod^fg_A / Mod^fg_{A, torsion} ≌ Coh(𝒪_X)`

Let `A` be a graded ring whose degree-zero part `A₀` is Noetherian and which is generated by
finitely many elements of `A₁` over `A₀`, and let `X = Proj A`. Stacks 0BXD asserts that `M ↦ M̃`
induces an **equivalence**

`Mod^fg_A / Mod^fg_{A, torsion} ⟶ Coh(𝒪_X)`

with quasi-inverse `ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))`. This file proves it.

Everything but the hypotheses of the source is derived rather than assumed: `A` is Noetherian and
of finite type over `A₀`, `Proj A` is quasi-compact, `A` is generated by the whole of `A₁` over
`A₀`, and the standard opens of the degree-one elements cover `Proj A`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTruncation` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegTruncationι`: the degree-`≥ 0`
  truncation `M_{≥ 0}` of a finitely generated graded module and its inclusion, in `Mod^fg_A`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.canonicalTwistedComparison` and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.nonnegComparison`: the map of Equation 01MR
  read in `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, M̃(n))`, and its corestriction
  `M_{≥ 0} ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, M̃(n))` in `Mod^fg_A`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.serreEquivalence`: **the equivalence of
  Stacks 0BXD**, with `M ↦ M̃` for its functor and `ℱ ↦ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, ℱ(n))` for its inverse on
  the nose.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.serreEquivalenceFunctorFac`: the equivalence
  is *induced* by `M ↦ M̃` — its composite with the quotient functor is the associated-sheaf
  functor on `Mod^fg_A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence`
  `.isIso_toIrrelevantQuotient_map_nonnegComparison`: the comparison
  `M_{≥ 0} ⟶ ⨁_{n ≥ 0} Γ(X, M̃(n))` becomes an isomorphism in the quotient category.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.essSurj_nonnegTwistedSectionsQuotientFunctor`
  and
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence`
  `.isEquivalence_nonnegTwistedSectionsQuotientFunctor`: the candidate quasi-inverse is
  essentially surjective, hence an equivalence.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.equivalence_coherentQuotientFunctor`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0BXD]**, the whole proposition.

## Implementation notes

**The comparison is read on the twisted side.** The quasi-inverse is built from
`⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, M̃(n))`, whereas Equation 01MR lands in `⨁_{n ∈ ℤ} Γ(X, M(n)~)`. The two graded
`A`-modules are identified by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjSerreCorrespondence.twistedShiftedGradedIso`, Tag 0B5R (3) at the
degree-one covering hypothesis, and `canonicalTwistedComparison` is Equation 01MR composed with
the inverse of that identification.

**The generating family.** "Generated by finitely many elements of `A₁`" is carried as a family
`x : Fin m → A` with `m` arbitrary, the empty family included.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXD](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXD)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BXE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BXE)
